There are no trials in this search yet. Earlier searches ran 84 trials and every one scored 0 on both dev and training success, so the agent never completes an exact build. That points to optimisation, exploration and inductive bias, not generalisation. One likely cause: the dense reward also pays for partly wrong or sealing bricks, so the +1 exact-build bonus is rarely or never seen. To see it, the policy needs sharper per-brick accuracy (lower entropy), longer credit horizons (gamma 0.995, high lambda) and many updates. While everything scores 0, I'm using breadth and stacking. All 6 candidates add the untested hygiene changes: orthogonal init, near-uniform starting policy (output gain 0.01), GroupNorm, a learned raw-obs skip into the footprint head, factorised type+anchor logits, and a DONE head that sees max-pooled learned projections of the obs. They differ in trunk (residual CNN, per-cell deep MLP, attention), head (pooled, per-cell concat, plus dense) and recipe extremes (1 epoch with 64-step rollouts at lr 3e-3; many tiny minibatches; no entropy bonus).

### Round 2
All six round-1 stacks scored 0 on dev and 0 on training success, as did the starting net. The stacks covered orthogonal init with near-uniform logits, GroupNorm, a raw skip, factorised logits, per-cell footprint heads, a column MLP, attention and recipe extremes. So the agent never completes an exact build even while training. That is an optimisation and inductive-bias problem, not a generalisation problem. Three gaps are still untested. (1) DONE has to fire exactly when no good placement is left, but it is rarely sampled at that moment. A DONE head that reads statistics of the placement logits can learn this comparison directly. (2) If the world's action layout differs from its description, every local head is misaligned. A zero-initialised learned remap of all placement logits could correct that. (3) Multiplicative stems express conjunctions easily, for example 'missing at layer l AND filled at l-1'. Below I stack these with different recipes: myopic, big-batch, 1 epoch and 3 epochs.

### Round 3
All 12 trials in this search scored 0 on dev and on training success, as did the 84 trials before them. So the agent never completes an exact build even on training designs. That points to slow learning or blocked learning, not poor generalisation.

These ideas have now failed as stacks:
